COURAGE BEYOND RANK: MAJOR GENERAL INUWA MAKES HISTORY WITH LANDMARK PARACHUTE JUMP

A Powerful Demonstration of Courage, Professional Excellence and Leadership by Example

In a remarkable demonstration of courage, discipline and professional excellence, Major General Muhammad Nura Inuwa, Commandant of the Nigerian Army School of Infantry (NASI), Jaji, Kaduna State, has reportedly achieved a historic milestone by successfully undertaking a static-line parachute jump from an aircraft on Wednesday, 21 October 2026.

Described as the first Nigerian Army Major General to accomplish this feat, the achievement represents more than a daring descent from thousands of feet above the ground. It reflects the enduring spirit of military professionalism, the importance of continuous training and the courage to embrace demanding challenges in the pursuit of excellence.

For a senior military officer entrusted with shaping the skills, discipline and operational readiness of soldiers, such an accomplishment sends a powerful message: leadership is not defined by rank alone, but by courage, competence and the willingness to lead by example.

The successful jump underscores the significance of physical preparedness, mental resilience, confidence and mastery of military skills. It also reinforces the principle that professional excellence requires continuous self-development, regardless of position or years of service.

As Commandant of NASI, Major General Inuwa occupies a strategic position in the development of infantry capabilities and the preparation of personnel for the complex demands of modern military operations. His reported achievement therefore serves as an inspiring reminder of the values the Nigerian Army continues to uphold—courage, discipline, determination and an unwavering commitment to duty.

Beyond the personal accomplishment, this milestone offers an enduring lesson to military personnel and aspiring leaders alike: true leadership inspires confidence, challenges limitations and demonstrates through action the standards expected of others.

Major General Muhammad Nura Inuwa: a testament to courage beyond rank, excellence beyond expectation, and leadership through personal example.

Service. Courage. Excellence. Leadership.
